{- | The LSP differential suite — every request set, every golden — as one
   runner over a table of properties.

   Three shell gates used to do this, 1,083 lines between them, each carrying
   its own copy of the same four mechanisms: frame a JSON-RPC message with a
   byte-counted `Content-Length`, feed the whole framed stream to one
   `medaka lsp` process, split the framed responses back apart, and compare
   the decoded objects against a committed golden. The mechanisms are the
   loop; the REQUESTS and what each answer has to say are the data. The rows
   here name them:

   | row | request set | what it pins |
   |---|---|---|
   | `initialize` | `initialize` with bare `{}` params | a JSON-RPC 2.0 result advertising `textDocumentSync`, from a server calling itself `medaka-lsp` |
   | `didopen-clean` | didOpen a clean buffer | `publishDiagnostics []`, agreeing with `medaka check --json` on the same source |
   | `didopen-type-error` | didOpen a buffer with a type error | one severity-1 `medaka` diagnostic whose expr-level range START and END are `check --json`'s |
   | `didchange-clean-to-error` | didOpen clean, then didChange to an error | two publishes, the second carrying the diagnostic the first did not |
   | `project-didopen` | didOpen a 3-module project's entry | one publish per file in the import graph, the bad import not blanking its clean siblings |
   | `b3-providers` | `initialize` | the four B.10.3 providers, and sync mode 1 |
   | `b3-documentsymbol` | didOpen, documentSymbol | every decl's name, `SymbolKind` and start line, children included |
   | `b3-definition` | didOpen, definition at the `area` decl | the defining decl's uri and start line |
   | `b3-documenthighlight` | didOpen, documentHighlight at `area` | each occurrence's FULL range, start and end |
   | `b3-formatting` | didOpen an unformatted buffer, formatting | one whole-document `TextEdit` whose `newText` is `medaka fmt`'s answer |
   | `b3-formatting-clean` | didOpen a formatted buffer, formatting | `[]` — an already-formatted document earns no edit |
   | `b4-providers` | `initialize` | hover, completion and inlayHint are advertised |
   | `b4-hover` | didOpen, hover on `double` | a Markdown `name : type`, rendered by `ppScheme` |
   | `b4-hover-off-identifier` | didOpen, hover on `=` | `null`, not the nearest identifier |
   | `b4-completion-prefix` | didOpen, completion after `doub` | the prefix-filtered candidate set, with kinds and details |
   | `b4-completion-empty-prefix` | didOpen, completion at column 0 | the WHOLE typecheck env, this buffer's own names included |
   | `b4-inlayhint` | didOpen, inlayHint over the buffer | one `: <ty>` hint per UNSIGNATURED top-level binding, at the real end-of-name column |
   | `b4-hover-shadowed-local` | didOpen, hover on a local shadowing a prelude name | the LOCAL's type (#2092, an S0: the prelude's scheme was answered instead) |
   | `b4-hover-no-local-control` | didOpen, hover where no local is in scope | the PRELUDE's scheme — proving #2092's fix is position-scoped, not "locals always win" |

   Each row is its own `medaka lsp` process, exactly as the retired scripts
   drove them: a session is one framed stream in and one framed stream out,
   so a row cannot inherit another row's server state.

   # What this grades that the retired scripts did not

   The scripts split the response stream on a `Content-Length: \d+` REGEX and
   then decoded whatever JSON followed, so the declared byte count was never
   read back. `decodeFrames` below consumes exactly the declared number of
   BYTES per frame and requires the next frame's header to begin where that
   count lands — a server that miscounts a multi-byte diagnostic desyncs the
   stream and fails the row it broke, rather than being re-synchronized by
   the regex and passing.

   The scripts also sent every spawn's stderr to `/dev/null` and read only
   the decoded stdout. This grades the exit code and stderr too (#2890): a
   server that answered correctly on its way out of a panic, or one printing
   the CLI's own staleness warning, has not passed.

   # What is NOT here

   `lsp.sh`'s seventh property — a multi-module project driven through seven
   `didChange` states, each compared against a COLD `medaka check --json` —
   needs the two disk edits to land BETWEEN messages of ONE session, which a
   single pre-framed stdin stream cannot express. Medaka's only process
   extern is `runCommand` (`stdlib/runtime.mdk`), which runs a command to
   completion with no stdin handle, so there is no native spelling of an
   interactive session. That property keeps its interactive driver in
   `test/lsp_warm_session.sh` and is graded here as its own test, on the
   script's exit code and output.

   # The goldens

   `test/lsp_goldens/` is READ here, never written. `check_{clean,err,
   project}.json` are `medaka check --json` over the same sources — a
   cross-check against a different code path, not a capture of the server
   under test. The `b3_*`/`b4_*` files are raw protocol dumps with no
   independent oracle, so blessing one enshrines whatever the server printed
   and is a decision to review by hand. Re-minting any of them is
   `test/lsp_bless.sh`; the last test below holds its golden list to the one
   these rows read, so a golden cannot lose its re-mint path in silence.

   Runs under `medaka test --native`: it spawns `medaka lsp` and reads the
   goldens, neither of which the interpreter binds. -}

import array as A
import compiler_cli_test_support.{
  boundedInTree, chompNewlines, summarizeSweep, sweepUnits
}
import fs.{mkdirAll}
import json.{
  JArray,
  JBool,
  JInt,
  JNull,
  JString,
  Json,
  asInt,
  asString,
  get,
  jArray,
  jObject,
  parse,
  stringify,
}
import list.{nub, reverse, somes, sort}
import path.{basename}
import string.{contains, join, lines, startsWith, trim, unlines}
import test.{fail, pass}
import test_process.{medakaBin, medakaRoot}

-- # Framing

{- | One Content-Length-framed JSON-RPC packet.

   The header's count is a BYTE count, so it comes from the UTF-8 encoding
   and never from `stringLength`, which counts codepoints: a request carrying
   one multi-byte character would otherwise declare a length short of its own
   body and desync the server on the first frame. -}
frame : Json -> String
frame msg =
  let body = stringify msg
  "Content-Length: \{intToString (utf8Len body)}\r\n\r\n\{body}"

utf8Len : String -> Int
utf8Len s = arrayLength (stringToUtf8Bytes s)

-- # Decoding

headerBytes : Array Int
headerBytes = stringToUtf8Bytes "Content-Length: "

separatorBytes : Array Int
separatorBytes = stringToUtf8Bytes "\r\n\r\n"

{- | The JSON objects of a framed JSON-RPC response stream, or an `Err`
   naming the byte offset where the framing stopped making sense.

   Strict by construction: each frame's declared count is consumed exactly,
   and the bytes that follow must begin the next header or end the stream.
   A declared count that does not match the body therefore fails here rather
   than being re-synchronized. -}
decodeFrames : String -> Result String (List Json)
decodeFrames out = framesFrom (stringToUtf8Bytes out) 0 []

framesFrom : Array Int -> Int -> List Json -> Result String (List Json)
framesFrom bs i acc
  | i >= arrayLength bs = Ok (reverse acc)
  | not (matchesAt bs i headerBytes) =
    Err
      "byte \{intToString i}: expected a Content-Length header, found \{debug (peek bs i)}"
  | otherwise = match digitsAt bs (i + arrayLength headerBytes)
    None => Err "byte \{intToString i}: Content-Length carries no digits"
    Some (declared, afterDigits) =>
      if not (matchesAt bs afterDigits separatorBytes) then
        Err
          "byte \{intToString afterDigits}: Content-Length is not followed by a blank line"
      else
        bodyFrom bs declared (afterDigits + arrayLength separatorBytes) acc

bodyFrom : Array Int -> Int -> Int -> List Json -> Result String (List Json)
bodyFrom bs declared start acc =
  let stop = start + declared
  if stop > arrayLength bs then
    Err
      "byte \{intToString start}: the frame declares \{intToString declared} bytes but only \{intToString (arrayLength bs - start)} remain"
  else match parse (stringFromUtf8Bytes (A.sliceClamped start stop bs))
    Err e =>
      Err
        "byte \{intToString start}: the \{intToString declared} bytes the frame declares are not one JSON value: \{e}"
    Ok j => framesFrom bs stop (j :: acc)

-- | The byte at `i`, or `-1` past either end, so a scan never has to bound
-- itself twice.
byteAt : Array Int -> Int -> Int
byteAt bs i = match A.get i bs
  Some b => b
  None => -1

matchesAt : Array Int -> Int -> Array Int -> Bool
matchesAt bs i pat = matchesFrom bs i pat 0

matchesFrom : Array Int -> Int -> Array Int -> Int -> Bool
matchesFrom bs i pat j
  | j >= arrayLength pat = True
  | byteAt bs (i + j) /= byteAt pat j = False
  | otherwise = matchesFrom bs i pat (j + 1)

-- | The decimal run at `i` and the index just past it, or `None` when `i`
-- is not a digit.
digitsAt : Array Int -> Int -> Option (Int, Int)
digitsAt bs i =
  if isDigitByte (byteAt bs i) then Some (digitsFrom bs i 0) else None

digitsFrom : Array Int -> Int -> Int -> (Int, Int)
digitsFrom bs i acc =
  let b = byteAt bs i
  if isDigitByte b then
    digitsFrom bs (i + 1) (acc * 10 + (b - 48))
  else
    (acc, i)

isDigitByte : Int -> Bool
isDigitByte b = b >= 48 && b <= 57

-- | A short excerpt for a framing failure's message.
peek : Array Int -> Int -> String
peek bs i = stringFromUtf8Bytes (A.sliceClamped i (i + 48) bs)

-- # Reading a response apart

-- | The value at a path of object keys, or `None` at the first key that is
-- absent or whose parent is not an object.
dig : List String -> Json -> Option Json
dig [] j = Some j
dig (k :: rest) j = match get k j
  None => None
  Some v => dig rest v

-- | The response object carrying `id`, or `None` when the server never
-- answered that request.
replyTo : Int -> List Json -> Option Json
replyTo idn objs = match filter (o => get "id" o == Some (JInt idn)) objs
  o :: _ => Some o
  [] => None

{- | The `result` of the reply to `id`.

   `Some JNull` (the server answered `null`) and `None` (the server did not
   answer at all) are different outcomes, and `textDocument/hover` off an
   identifier is specified to produce the first. -}
resultTo : Int -> List Json -> Option Json
resultTo idn objs = match replyTo idn objs
  None => None
  Some o => get "result" o

publishes : List Json -> List Json
publishes objs =
  filter
    (o => get "method" o == Some (JString "textDocument/publishDiagnostics"))
    objs

-- | The elements of a JSON array, or `[]` for anything else.
elems : Option Json -> List Json
elems (Some (JArray a)) = toList a
elems _ = []

diagsOf : Json -> List Json
diagsOf pub = elems (dig ["params", "diagnostics"] pub)

uriOf : Json -> String
uriOf pub = match dig ["params", "uri"] pub
  Some (JString u) => u
  _ => ""

strField : String -> Json -> String
strField k j = match get k j
  Some (JString s) => s
  _ => ""

intField : String -> Json -> Int
intField k j = match get k j
  Some (JInt n) => n
  _ => -1

-- | `line:character` of one end of a range, or a legible stand-in.
endpoint : String -> Json -> String
endpoint which j = match dig ["range", which] j
  None => "(no \{which})"
  Some p =>
    "\{intToString (intField "line" p)}:\{intToString (intField "character" p)}"

-- | One diagnostic's severity and start, as a sortable line. The MESSAGE is
-- deliberately absent: it is prose that reorders with unification order, the
-- documented divergence the retired gates also declined to diff.
diagKey : Json -> String
diagKey d =
  "severity \{intToString (intField "severity" d)} at \{endpoint "start" d}"

-- | `Some msg` when the claim does not hold — the shape `somes` collects.
unless : Bool -> String -> Option String
unless ok msg = if ok then None else Some msg

-- # The request sets

rpc : Int -> String -> Json -> Json
rpc idn method params = jObject [
  ("jsonrpc", JString "2.0"),
  ("id", JInt idn),
  ("method", JString method),
  ("params", params),
]

notify : String -> Json -> Json
notify method params = jObject [
  ("jsonrpc", JString "2.0"),
  ("method", JString method),
  ("params", params),
]

{- | `initialize` with bare `{}` params.

   The empty params are the assertion: `InitializeParams` has no required
   member the server needs, and a server that fataled without a
   `capabilities` object would reject an editor that sent none. -}
initBare : Json
initBare = rpc 1 "initialize" (jObject [])

initCaps : Json
initCaps = rpc 1 "initialize" (jObject [("capabilities", jObject [])])

inited : Json
inited = notify "initialized" (jObject [])

bye : Json
bye = notify "exit" (jObject [])

{- | `textDocument/didOpen` carrying a whole `TextDocumentItem`.

   All four members are sent, `languageId` and `version` included: they are
   required by the protocol, and two of the retired scripts already sent
   them. -}
didOpenMsg : String -> String -> Json
didOpenMsg uri text =
  notify
    "textDocument/didOpen"
    (jObject [
      (
        "textDocument",
        jObject [
          ("uri", JString uri),
          ("languageId", JString "medaka"),
          ("version", JInt 1),
          ("text", JString text),
        ],
      ),
    ])

-- | `textDocument/didChange` under Full sync: the whole document is replaced.
didChangeMsg : String -> String -> Json
didChangeMsg uri text =
  notify
    "textDocument/didChange"
    (jObject [
      ("textDocument", jObject [("uri", JString uri), ("version", JInt 2)]),
      ("contentChanges", jArray [jObject [("text", JString text)]]),
    ])

docParams : String -> Json
docParams uri = jObject [("textDocument", jObject [("uri", JString uri)])]

posParams : String -> Int -> Int -> Json
posParams uri line ch = jObject [
  ("textDocument", jObject [("uri", JString uri)]),
  ("position", jObject [("line", JInt line), ("character", JInt ch)]),
]

-- # The sources each row opens

cleanSrc : String
cleanSrc = "main = println \"hi\"\n"

errSrc : String
errSrc = "main = 1 + \"x\"\n"

{- | A record decl, a sum decl and a function — the shapes `documentSymbol`
   has to render as a symbol with children, a symbol with none, and a
   function. -}
symSrc : String
symSrc =
  "data Point = { x : Int, y : Int }\n\ndata Shape = Circle Int | Square Int\n\narea s = match s\n  Circle r => r * r\n  Square w => w * w\n"

-- | Extra spaces and trailing blank lines, all of which `medaka fmt` removes.
unformattedSrc : String
unformattedSrc = "main   =   println    \"hi\"\n\n\n"

{- | One unsignatured binding, one signatured one, a use, and an
   `export`-prefixed binding.

   The `export quad` line is the discriminating one for `inlayHint`: its
   name ENDS at column 11, while a heuristic scanning the leading identifier
   run from column 0 would stop after `export`, at column 6. Every other
   line here begins its name at column 0 and cannot tell the two apart.
   (`public export` is not available: `public` alone is a data-only modifier,
   so a value binding can only be `export`-prefixed.) -}
b4Src : String
b4Src =
  "double x = x + x\ntriple : Int -> Int\ntriple x = x * 3\nresult = double 5\nexport quad x = x * 4\n"

-- | Two top-level names, for the empty-prefix completion row to find among
-- the whole prelude env.
b4NamesSrc : String
b4NamesSrc = "alpha = 1\nbeta = 2\n\n"

-- | A local binding shadowing the prelude's `count` (#2092).
shadowSrc : String
shadowSrc = "main =\n  let count = 5\n  println count\n"

-- | The same name with NO local in scope — the prelude's `count` is the
-- right answer here.
noLocalSrc : String
noLocalSrc = "main = println (count (x => x > 1) [1, 2, 3])\n"

{- | A `count` local in an EARLIER decl, and a prelude `count` use in a later
   one.

   A name-only preference — "a local named `count` exists in this buffer" —
   would answer `Int` for the second decl. Only a position-scoped one
   answers the prelude's scheme. -}
crossDeclSrc : String
crossDeclSrc =
  "f =\n  let count = 5\n  println count\n\nmain = println (count (x => x > 1) [1, 2, 3])\n"

-- # The project one row opens

libCleanSrc : String
libCleanSrc = "export double : Int -> Int\ndouble x = x + x\n"

libBadSrc : String
libBadSrc =
  "import lib_clean.{double}\n\nexport oops : Int\noops = double \"no\"\n"

mainAppSrc : String
mainAppSrc =
  "import lib_clean.{double}\nimport lib_bad.{oops}\n\nmain = println (double 21)\n"

projectFiles : List (String, String)
projectFiles = [
  ("lib_clean.mdk", libCleanSrc),
  ("lib_bad.mdk", libBadSrc),
  ("main_app.mdk", mainAppSrc),
]

-- # The table

{- | The golden a row reads, and how to read it.

   - `NoOracle` — the row's expected values are decided from the source, so
     there is nothing a re-capture could bless away.
   - `Frames f` — `test/lsp_goldens/<f>`, one JSON object per line.
   - `Text f` — `test/lsp_goldens/<f>`, read verbatim. -}
data Oracle = NoOracle | Frames String | Text String

{- | One property: the session that provokes it, the golden it reads, and
   what the answer has to say.

   `requests` takes the row's own scratch directory because one row opens a
   project whose `file://` uris only exist once that directory does; every
   other row ignores it. `files` is what gets written there first, relative
   to it. -}
data Probe = Probe {
  name : String,
  files : List (String, String),
  requests : String -> List Json,
  oracle : Oracle,
  grade : Seen -> List String,
}

{- | One session as its grader sees it: the decoded responses, the golden's
   frames, and the golden's raw text. -}
data Seen = Seen { objs : List Json, gold : List Json, goldText : String }

probes : List Probe
probes = [
  Probe {
    name = "initialize",
    files = [],
    requests = _ => [initBare, bye],
    oracle = NoOracle,
    grade = gradeInitialize,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "didopen-clean",
    files = [],
    requests =
      _ => [
        initBare,
        didOpenMsg "file:///clean.mdk" cleanSrc,
        bye,
      ],
    oracle = Frames "check_clean.json",
    grade = gradeClean,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "didopen-type-error",
    files = [],
    requests = _ => [initBare, didOpenMsg "file:///err.mdk" errSrc, bye],
    oracle = Frames "check_err.json",
    grade = gradeTypeError,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "didchange-clean-to-error",
    files = [],
    requests =
      _ => [
        initBare,
        didOpenMsg "file:///d.mdk" cleanSrc,
        didChangeMsg "file:///d.mdk" errSrc,
        bye,
      ],
    oracle = NoOracle,
    grade = gradeDidChange,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "project-didopen",
    files = projectFiles,
    requests =
      dir => [
        initBare,
        didOpenMsg "file://\{dir}/main_app.mdk" mainAppSrc,
        bye,
      ],
    oracle = Frames "check_project.json",
    grade = gradeProject,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b3-providers",
    files = [],
    requests = _ => [initCaps, bye],
    oracle = NoOracle,
    grade = gradeProviders b3Providers,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b3-documentsymbol",
    files = [],
    requests = _ => b3Session,
    oracle = Frames "b3_sym_def_hl.ndjson",
    grade = gradeDocumentSymbol,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b3-definition",
    files = [],
    requests = _ => b3Session,
    oracle = Frames "b3_sym_def_hl.ndjson",
    grade = gradeDefinition,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b3-documenthighlight",
    files = [],
    requests = _ => b3Session,
    oracle = Frames "b3_sym_def_hl.ndjson",
    grade = gradeHighlight,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b3-formatting",
    files = [],
    requests =
      _ => [
        initCaps,
        inited,
        didOpenMsg "file:///u.mdk" unformattedSrc,
        rpc 2 "textDocument/formatting" (docParams "file:///u.mdk"),
        bye,
      ],
    oracle = Text "b3_fmt.txt",
    grade = gradeFormatting,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b3-formatting-clean",
    files = [],
    requests =
      _ => [
        initCaps,
        inited,
        didOpenMsg "file:///f.mdk" cleanSrc,
        rpc 2 "textDocument/formatting" (docParams "file:///f.mdk"),
        bye,
      ],
    oracle = NoOracle,
    grade = gradeFormattingClean,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b4-providers",
    files = [],
    requests = _ => [initCaps, bye],
    oracle = NoOracle,
    grade = gradeProviders b4Providers,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b4-hover",
    files = [],
    requests =
      _ => [
        initCaps,
        didOpenMsg "file:///b4.mdk" b4Src,
        rpc 2 "textDocument/hover" (posParams "file:///b4.mdk" 0 2),
        bye,
      ],
    oracle = Frames "b4_hover.ndjson",
    grade = gradeHover,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b4-hover-off-identifier",
    files = [],
    requests =
      _ => [
        initCaps,
        didOpenMsg "file:///b4.mdk" b4Src,
        rpc 2 "textDocument/hover" (posParams "file:///b4.mdk" 0 9),
        bye,
      ],
    oracle = Frames "b4_hover_off.ndjson",
    grade = gradeHoverOff,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b4-completion-prefix",
    files = [],
    requests =
      _ => [
        initCaps,
        didOpenMsg "file:///b4.mdk" b4Src,
        rpc 3 "textDocument/completion" (posParams "file:///b4.mdk" 3 13),
        bye,
      ],
    oracle = Frames "b4_compl.ndjson",
    grade = gradeCompletionPrefix,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b4-completion-empty-prefix",
    files = [],
    requests =
      _ => [
        initCaps,
        didOpenMsg "file:///b4b.mdk" b4NamesSrc,
        rpc 3 "textDocument/completion" (posParams "file:///b4b.mdk" 2 0),
        bye,
      ],
    oracle = Frames "b4_compl_full.ndjson",
    grade = gradeCompletionFull,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b4-inlayhint",
    files = [],
    requests =
      _ => [
        initCaps,
        didOpenMsg "file:///b4.mdk" b4Src,
        rpc 4 "textDocument/inlayHint" (inlayParams "file:///b4.mdk"),
        bye,
      ],
    oracle = Frames "b4_inlay.ndjson",
    grade = gradeInlay,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b4-hover-shadowed-local",
    files = [],
    requests =
      _ => [
        initCaps,
        didOpenMsg "file:///b4shadow.mdk" shadowSrc,
        rpc 7 "textDocument/hover" (posParams "file:///b4shadow.mdk" 2 11),
        rpc 8 "textDocument/hover" (posParams "file:///b4shadow.mdk" 1 7),
        bye,
      ],
    oracle = NoOracle,
    grade = gradeShadowedLocal,
  },
  Probe {
    name = "b4-hover-no-local-control",
    files = [],
    requests =
      _ => [
        initCaps,
        didOpenMsg "file:///b4noloc.mdk" noLocalSrc,
        rpc 9 "textDocument/hover" (posParams "file:///b4noloc.mdk" 0 17),
        didOpenMsg "file:///b4xdecl.mdk" crossDeclSrc,
        rpc 10 "textDocument/hover" (posParams "file:///b4xdecl.mdk" 4 17),
        bye,
      ],
    oracle = NoOracle,
    grade = gradeNoLocalControl,
  },
]

-- | The three B.10.3 queries share one buffer and one session; splitting
-- them into three rows keeps each answer's failure its own, without paying
-- three spawns for one didOpen.
b3Session : List Json
b3Session = [
  initCaps,
  inited,
  didOpenMsg "file:///s.mdk" symSrc,
  rpc 2 "textDocument/documentSymbol" (docParams "file:///s.mdk"),
  rpc 3 "textDocument/definition" (posParams "file:///s.mdk" 4 0),
  rpc 4 "textDocument/documentHighlight" (posParams "file:///s.mdk" 4 0),
  rpc 9 "shutdown" (jObject []),
  bye,
]

inlayParams : String -> Json
inlayParams uri = jObject [
  ("textDocument", jObject [("uri", JString uri)]),
  (
    "range",
    jObject [
      ("start", jObject [("line", JInt 0), ("character", JInt 0)]),
      ("end", jObject [("line", JInt 10), ("character", JInt 0)]),
    ],
  ),
]

{- | A capability roster: the key, and either the value it must carry or
   `None` for "advertised at all".

   `completionProvider` is the one that cannot be spelled as a value — it is
   a `CompletionOptions` object, and an editor reads its presence, not its
   contents. -}
b3Providers : List (String, Option Json)
b3Providers = [
  ("textDocumentSync", Some (JInt 1)),
  ("documentFormattingProvider", Some (JBool True)),
  ("documentSymbolProvider", Some (JBool True)),
  ("definitionProvider", Some (JBool True)),
  ("documentHighlightProvider", Some (JBool True)),
]

b4Providers : List (String, Option Json)
b4Providers = [
  ("hoverProvider", Some (JBool True)),
  ("completionProvider", None),
  ("inlayHintProvider", Some (JBool True)),
]

-- # The graders

gradeInitialize : Seen -> List String
gradeInitialize s = match replyTo 1 s.objs
  None => ["the server never answered the initialize request"]
  Some init => somes [
    unless
      (get "jsonrpc" init == Some (JString "2.0"))
      "the reply is not JSON-RPC 2.0",
    unless (get "result" init /= None) "the reply carries no result",
    unless
      (dig ["result", "capabilities", "textDocumentSync"] init /= None)
      "the capabilities do not advertise textDocumentSync",
    unless
      (dig ["result", "serverInfo", "name"] init == Some (JString "medaka-lsp"))
      "serverInfo.name is not \"medaka-lsp\"",
  ]

gradeProviders : List (String, Option Json) -> Seen -> List String
gradeProviders wanted s = match dig ["result", "capabilities"] (initReply s)
  None => ["the initialize reply carries no capabilities"]
  Some caps => somes (map (advertised caps) wanted)

initReply : Seen -> Json
initReply s = match replyTo 1 s.objs
  Some init => init
  None => JNull

advertised : Json -> (String, Option Json) -> Option String
advertised caps (key, want) = match get key caps
  None => Some "the capabilities do not advertise \{key}"
  Some got => match want
    None => None
    Some v =>
      unless (got == v) "\{key} is \{stringify got}, expected \{stringify v}"

gradeClean : Seen -> List String
gradeClean s = match publishes s.objs
  [] => ["the server published no diagnostics for the opened buffer"]
  pub :: _ => somes [
    unless
      (diagsOf pub == [])
      "a clean buffer published \{intToString (length (diagsOf pub))} diagnostics",
    unless
      (oracleDiags s == [])
      "medaka check --json reports diagnostics on the same source, so the fixture is not clean",
  ]

gradeTypeError : Seen -> List String
gradeTypeError s = match publishes s.objs
  [] => ["the server published no diagnostics for the opened buffer"]
  pub :: _ => checkOneDiag (diagsOf pub) (oracleDiags s)

checkOneDiag : List Json -> List Json -> List String
checkOneDiag [d] [o] = somes [
  unless
    (intField "severity" d == 1)
    "the diagnostic's severity is not 1 (Error)",
  unless
    (intField "severity" o == 1)
    "check --json's diagnostic is not an error either, so the fixture proves nothing",
  unless
    (strField "source" d == "medaka")
    "the diagnostic's source is not \"medaka\"",
  unless
    (strField "source" o == "medaka")
    "check --json's diagnostic is not sourced \"medaka\" either, so the twin proves nothing",
  unless (get "message" d /= None) "the diagnostic carries no message",
  unless
    (endpoint "start" d == endpoint "start" o)
    "range START is \{endpoint "start" d}, check --json says \{endpoint "start" o}",
  unless
    (endpoint "end" d == endpoint "end" o)
    "range END is \{endpoint "end" d}, check --json says \{endpoint "end" o}",
]
checkOneDiag ds os = [
  "expected one diagnostic on each side, got \{intToString (length ds)} published and \{intToString (length os)} from check --json",
]

gradeDidChange : Seen -> List String
gradeDidChange s = match publishes s.objs
  [first, second] => somes [
    unless
      (diagsOf first == [])
      "the didOpen of a clean buffer published a diagnostic",
    unless
      (length (diagsOf second) == 1)
      "the didChange to an ill-typed buffer published \{intToString (length (diagsOf second))} diagnostics, expected 1",
    unless
      (all (d => intField "severity" d == 1) (diagsOf second))
      "the republished diagnostic is not an error",
  ]
  pubs => [
    "expected two publishes — one per notification — got \{intToString (length pubs)}",
  ]

gradeProject : Seen -> List String
gradeProject s =
  let mine =
    map (p => perFile (basename (uriOf p)) (diagsOf p)) (publishes s.objs)
  let theirs =
    map (f => perFile (strField "file" f) (oracleFileDiags f)) (oracleFilesOf s)
  somes [
    unless
      (sort mine == sort theirs)
      "the published diagnostics differ from check --json's\n  published:\n\{indentAll (sort mine)}  check --json:\n\{indentAll (sort theirs)}",
    unless
      (elem (perFile "lib_clean.mdk" []) mine)
      "lib_clean.mdk was not published clean — a bad import blanked a clean sibling",
    unless
      (elem (perFile "main_app.mdk" []) mine)
      "main_app.mdk was not published clean — a bad import blanked the entry",
    unless
      (not (elem (perFile "lib_bad.mdk" []) mine))
      "lib_bad.mdk was published clean — its diagnostic was lost",
  ]

-- | One file's published diagnostics as a sortable line.
perFile : String -> List Json -> String
perFile file diags = "\{file} -> [\{join ", " (sort (map diagKey diags))}]"

oracleFilesOf : Seen -> List Json
oracleFilesOf s = match s.gold
  doc :: _ => elems (get "files" doc)
  [] => []

oracleFileDiags : Json -> List Json
oracleFileDiags f = elems (get "diagnostics" f)

-- | The diagnostics of the FIRST file of a `medaka check --json` document —
-- the whole of a single-file check.
oracleDiags : Seen -> List Json
oracleDiags s = match oracleFilesOf s
  f :: _ => oracleFileDiags f
  [] => []

indentAll : List String -> String
indentAll ls = unlines (map (l => "    \{l}") ls)

{- | A symbol's name, kind and start line, with its children — the decl-level
   skeleton.

   END lines are not compared: the AST's per-decl end is its last content
   token, so a decl followed by blank lines ends earlier than an editor's
   own notion of the decl's extent. The `detail` an outline may carry is
   additive and not compared either. -}
symbolSkeleton : Json -> String
symbolSkeleton sym =
  let kids = elems (get "children" sym)
  "\{strField "name" sym}:\{intToString (intField "kind" sym)}@\{startLine sym}(\{join "," (map symbolSkeleton kids)})"

startLine : Json -> String
startLine j = match dig ["range", "start", "line"] j
  Some (JInt n) => intToString n
  _ => "(no start line)"

gradeDocumentSymbol : Seen -> List String
gradeDocumentSymbol s =
  let mine = map symbolSkeleton (elems (resultTo 2 s.objs))
  let theirs = map symbolSkeleton (elems (resultTo 2 s.gold))
  somes [
    unless (mine /= []) "documentSymbol returned no symbols at all",
    unless
      (mine == theirs)
      "the outline differs from the golden\n  got:  \{join " " mine}\n  want: \{join " " theirs}",
  ]

-- | A location's uri and start line — what "go to definition" lands on.
locationKey : Json -> String
locationKey loc = "\{strField "uri" loc}@\{startLine loc}"

gradeDefinition : Seen -> List String
gradeDefinition s =
  let mine = map locationKey (elems (resultTo 3 s.objs))
  let theirs = map locationKey (elems (resultTo 3 s.gold))
  somes [
    unless
      (mine == theirs)
      "definition differs from the golden: got \{debug mine}, want \{debug theirs}",
    unless
      (mine == ["file:///s.mdk@4"])
      "definition did not land on the `area` decl (line 4 of its own file): \{debug mine}",
  ]

-- | An occurrence's FULL range. Highlights are computed textually, so both
-- ends are exact and both are compared.
highlightKey : Json -> String
highlightKey h = "\{endpoint "start" h}-\{endpoint "end" h}"

gradeHighlight : Seen -> List String
gradeHighlight s =
  let mine = sort (map highlightKey (elems (resultTo 4 s.objs)))
  let theirs = sort (map highlightKey (elems (resultTo 4 s.gold)))
  somes [
    unless
      (mine == theirs)
      "documentHighlight differs from the golden: got \{debug mine}, want \{debug theirs}",
    unless
      (mine == ["4:0-4:4"])
      "`area` occurs once, spanning its four characters; got \{debug mine}",
  ]

gradeFormatting : Seen -> List String
gradeFormatting s = match elems (resultTo 2 s.objs)
  [edit] => somes [
    unless
      (chompNewlines (strField "newText" edit) == chompNewlines s.goldText)
      "the edit's newText is not what `medaka fmt` produces:\n    got:  \{debug (strField "newText" edit)}\n    want: \{debug s.goldText}",
    unless
      (dig ["range", "start"] edit
        == Some (jObject [("line", JInt 0), ("character", JInt 0)]))
      "the edit does not start at the top of the document",
  ]
  edits =>
    ["expected one whole-document TextEdit, got \{intToString (length edits)}"]

gradeFormattingClean : Seen -> List String
gradeFormattingClean s = somes [
  unless
    (resultTo 2 s.objs == Some (jArray []))
    "an already-formatted document earned an edit: \{debug (resultTo 2 s.objs)}",
]

-- | The rendered hover body of the reply to `id`, or `""`.
hoverValue : Int -> List Json -> String
hoverValue idn objs = match replyTo idn objs
  None => ""
  Some o => match dig ["result", "contents", "value"] o
    Some (JString v) => v
    _ => ""

hoverKind : Int -> List Json -> String
hoverKind idn objs = match replyTo idn objs
  None => ""
  Some o => match dig ["result", "contents", "kind"] o
    Some (JString k) => k
    _ => ""

{- | The WHOLE `contents` object of the reply to `id`, not one member of it.

   The golden comparison is phrased over this rather than over `.value`
   because a member ADDED to `contents` is invisible to a per-member
   comparison — the reply would grow a field the golden never recorded and
   every assertion would still hold. -}
hoverContents : Int -> List Json -> Option Json
hoverContents idn objs = match replyTo idn objs
  None => None
  Some o => dig ["result", "contents"] o

gradeHover : Seen -> List String
gradeHover s = somes [
  unless (hoverKind 2 s.objs == "markdown") "the hover body is not Markdown",
  unless
    (hoverContents 2 s.objs == hoverContents 2 s.gold)
    "the hover contents differ from the golden: got \{debug (hoverContents 2 s.objs)}, want \{debug (hoverContents 2 s.gold)}",
  unless
    (contains "double" (hoverValue 2 s.objs))
    "the hover body does not name `double`, so it is not this identifier's type",
]

gradeHoverOff : Seen -> List String
gradeHoverOff s = somes [
  unless
    (resultTo 2 s.objs == Some JNull)
    "hover off an identifier answered \{debug (resultTo 2 s.objs)}, expected null",
  unless
    (resultTo 2 s.gold == Some JNull)
    "the golden does not record a null there, so this row is comparing the wrong position",
]

{- | One completion candidate's label, kind and detail.

   Compared as a SET, never as a list: the env is walked in an order the
   protocol does not fix, and an editor sorts the items itself. -}
itemKey : Json -> String
itemKey it =
  "\{strField "label" it}:\{intToString (intField "kind" it)}:\{strField "detail" it}"

-- | A completion result is either the item list or a `CompletionList`
-- wrapping it; both spellings are legal and the server may use either.
itemsOf : Option Json -> List Json
itemsOf (Some (JArray a)) = toList a
itemsOf (Some o) = elems (get "items" o)
itemsOf None = []

gradeCompletionPrefix : Seen -> List String
gradeCompletionPrefix s =
  let mine = sort (map itemKey (itemsOf (resultTo 3 s.objs)))
  let theirs = sort (map itemKey (itemsOf (resultTo 3 s.gold)))
  somes [
    unless
      (mine == theirs)
      "the candidate set differs from the golden\n  got:  \{debug mine}\n  want: \{debug theirs}",
    unless
      (elem
        "double"
        (map (l => strField "label" l) (itemsOf (resultTo 3 s.objs))))
      "`double` is not among the candidates for the prefix `doub`",
    unless
      (all
        (l => startsWith "doub" (strField "label" l))
        (itemsOf (resultTo 3 s.objs)))
      "a candidate does not start with the prefix `doub`",
  ]

gradeCompletionFull : Seen -> List String
gradeCompletionFull s =
  let labels = map (l => strField "label" l) (itemsOf (resultTo 3 s.objs))
  somes [
    unless
      (sort (map itemKey (itemsOf (resultTo 3 s.objs)))
        == sort (map itemKey (itemsOf (resultTo 3 s.gold))))
      "the whole-env candidate set differs from the golden (\{intToString (length labels)} candidates here, \{intToString (length (itemsOf (resultTo 3 s.gold)))} there)",
    unless
      (elem "alpha" labels)
      "the buffer's own `alpha` is missing from the env",
    unless
      (elem "beta" labels)
      "the buffer's own `beta` is missing from the env",
  ]

-- | One hint's position, label and padding.
hintKey : Json -> String
hintKey h =
  "\{intToString (hintLine h)}:\{intToString (hintChar h)} \{debug (strField "label" h)} pad=\{debug (get "paddingLeft" h)}"

hintLine : Json -> Int
hintLine h = match dig ["position", "line"] h
  Some (JInt n) => n
  _ => -1

hintChar : Json -> Int
hintChar h = match dig ["position", "character"] h
  Some (JInt n) => n
  _ => -1

gradeInlay : Seen -> List String
gradeInlay s =
  let mine = elems (resultTo 4 s.objs)
  let onLine = n => filter (h => hintLine h == n) mine
  somes [
    unless
      (sort (map hintKey mine)
        == sort (map hintKey (elems (resultTo 4 s.gold))))
      "the hints differ from the golden\n  got:  \{debug (sort (map hintKey mine))}\n  want: \{debug (sort (map hintKey (elems (resultTo 4 s.gold))))}",
    unless (onLine 0 /= []) "the unsignatured `double` earned no hint",
    unless (onLine 1 == []) "the signature line of `triple` earned a hint",
    unless (onLine 2 == []) "the already-signatured `triple` earned a hint",
    unless
      (map hintChar (onLine 4) == [11])
      "the `export quad` hint sits at column \{debug (map hintChar (onLine 4))}, not 11 — the end of the NAME, not the end of the `export` keyword",
  ]

gradeShadowedLocal : Seen -> List String
gradeShadowedLocal s =
  somes (map (localIsInt s) [(7, "the use"), (8, "the binder")])

localIsInt : Seen -> (Int, String) -> Option String
localIsInt s (idn, which) =
  let v = hoverValue idn s.objs
  if contains "count : Int" v && not (contains "Foldable" v) then
    None
  else
    Some
      "\{which} of the local `count` hovers as \{debug v}, expected the local's own `count : Int`"

gradeNoLocalControl : Seen -> List String
gradeNoLocalControl s =
  somes
    (map (preludeScheme s) [
      (9, "with no local anywhere"),
      (10, "with a local in another decl"),
    ])

preludeScheme : Seen -> (Int, String) -> Option String
preludeScheme s (idn, which) =
  let v = hoverValue idn s.objs
  if contains "Foldable" v && not (contains "count : Int\n" v) then
    None
  else
    Some
      "`count` \{which} hovers as \{debug v}, expected the prelude's Foldable-constrained scheme"

-- # Running one row

{- | The ceiling on one session.

   A session that opens a project typechecks its whole import graph, and the
   whole-env completion row renders every prelude scheme, so the single-verb
   default in `test_process` is not a ceiling either can borrow. -}
sessionTimeoutSeconds : Int
sessionTimeoutSeconds = 180

{- | Drives one `medaka lsp` over the framed request stream, and grades the
   spawn itself: the findings it returns are about the PROCESS, and the string
   is its stdout for the row's own grader to read.

   The stream reaches the server's stdin through a `sh -c` redirect because
   `boundedVerb` has no stdin parameter; `printf '%s'` writes its argument
   with no escape processing, so the CR bytes the protocol requires survive
   verbatim. The pipeline's status is the server's own, which is what makes
   the exit code gradeable at all.

   A nonzero exit, a panic, or ANY stderr is a failure (#2890): `medaka lsp`
   speaks on stdout and says nothing on stderr, so a line there is the CLI's
   own staleness warning or a server that was not well — either of which makes
   every answer below untrustworthy however right it looks. -}
drive : List Json -> <Exec "_", IO> (List String, String)
drive msgs =
  let stream = join "" (map frame msgs)
  let args = ["-c", "printf '%s' \"$1\" | \"$2\" lsp", "sh", stream, medakaBin]
  match boundedInTree sessionTimeoutSeconds "sh" args
    Err e => (["could not spawn medaka lsp: \{e}"], "")
    Ok (code, out, err) =>
      let findings = somes [
        unless (code == 0) "medaka lsp exited \{intToString code}",
        unless
          (not (contains "E-PANIC" err))
          "medaka lsp panicked: \{debug err}",
        unless (err == "") "medaka lsp wrote to stderr: \{debug err}",
      ]
      (findings, out)

{- | One row's outcome. `findings` is the whole list rather than the first,
   so a red run names every disagreement at once. -}
data Outcome = Outcome { name : String, findings : List String }

gradeProbe : String ->
  Probe ->
  <Exec "_", FileRead "_", FileWrite "_", IO> Outcome
gradeProbe scratch p =
  let dir = "\{scratch}/\{p.name}"
  match layOut dir p.files
    Err e => Outcome { name = p.name, findings = [e] }
    Ok _ => match drive (p.requests dir)
      (spawned, out) =>
        Outcome { name = p.name, findings = spawned ++ decodeAndGrade p out }

{- | Writes a row's fixture files under its own directory.

   Each row gets its own, since one row's project is another row's noise:
   a leftover `main_app.mdk` in a shared directory would be read by whatever
   later row opened a buffer beside it. -}
layOut : String ->
  List (String, String) ->
  <FileWrite "_", IO> Result String Unit
layOut _ [] = Ok ()
layOut dir files = match mkdirAll dir
  Err e => Err "could not make \{dir}: \{e}"
  Ok _ => writeAll dir files

writeAll : String ->
  List (String, String) ->
  <FileWrite "_", IO> Result String Unit
writeAll _ [] = Ok ()
writeAll dir ((rel, text) :: rest) = match writeFile "\{dir}/\{rel}" text
  Err e => Err "could not write \{dir}/\{rel}: \{e}"
  Ok _ => writeAll dir rest

decodeAndGrade : Probe -> String -> <FileRead "_", IO> List String
decodeAndGrade p out = match decodeFrames out
  Err e => ["the response stream is not well framed: \{e}"]
  Ok objs => match readOracle p.oracle
    Err e => [e]
    Ok (gold, goldText) =>
      p.grade Seen { objs = objs, gold = gold, goldText = goldText }

readOracle : Oracle -> <FileRead "_", IO> Result String (List Json, String)
readOracle NoOracle = Ok ([], "")
readOracle (Text name) = map (text => ([], text)) (goldenText name)
readOracle (Frames name) = match goldenText name
  Err e => Err e
  Ok text => match parseLines (filter (l => trim l /= "") (lines text))
    Err e => Err "test/lsp_goldens/\{name}: \{e}"
    Ok objs => Ok (objs, text)

goldenText : String -> <FileRead "_", IO> Result String String
goldenText name = match readFile "\{medakaRoot}/test/lsp_goldens/\{name}"
  Err e => Err "could not read test/lsp_goldens/\{name}: \{e}"
  Ok text => Ok text

parseLines : List String -> Result String (List Json)
parseLines [] = Ok []
parseLines (l :: rest) = match parse l
  Err e => Err "a line is not JSON: \{e}"
  Ok j => map (j :: _) (parseLines rest)

probeFailure : Outcome -> Option String
probeFailure o = match o.findings
  [] => None
  fs =>
    Some "  \{o.name} (\{intToString (length fs)} findings):\n\{indentAll fs}"

test "every LSP request set answers as its golden and its source say" =
  sweepUnits probes gradeProbe probeFailure summarizeSweep

-- # The one session that cannot be pre-framed

{- | `lsp.sh`'s warm-versus-cold property, still driven by a script.

   Graded on the script's exit code AND its transcript, not on the code
   alone: the script prints one line per state and a `N ok, M failing`
   summary, and a run that reached no state at all would otherwise exit 0
   having proved nothing. -}
warmSessionScript : String
warmSessionScript = "test/lsp_warm_session.sh"

{- | Spawns the script with the shell in program position and the path as the
   first argument of the same call.

   Spelled inline rather than through a `let`-bound argument list because
   `test/diff_compiler_tier_drift.sh` reads this call to derive when
   `lsp_warm_session` runs — this module IS that gate's only invocation site,
   and a name in front of the list hides it. -}
runWarmSession : <Exec "_", IO> Result String (Int, String, String)
runWarmSession = boundedInTree sessionTimeoutSeconds "sh" [
  "\{medakaRoot}/\{warmSessionScript}",
]

test "a warm multi-module session publishes what a cold check --json reports" =
  match runWarmSession
    Err e => fail "could not run \{warmSessionScript}: \{e}"
    Ok (code, out, err) =>
      let text = out ++ err
      if code /= 0 then
        fail "\{warmSessionScript} exited \{intToString code}:\n\{text}"
      else if not (contains ", 0 failing" text) then
        fail
          "\{warmSessionScript} exited 0 without a passing summary — it may have graded nothing:\n\{text}"
      else
        pass

-- # Every golden this gate reads has a re-mint path

{- | The goldens `test/lsp_bless.sh` mints, from the sentinel-delimited list
   it carries, one name per line.

   The tool has to spell the sessions and sources that produce each golden,
   which is a second copy of this file's own table — but a copy that cannot
   rot in silence, because a golden minted from the WRONG session is one this
   gate then compares against and rejects on the next run. What a wrong copy
   CAN do quietly is mint nothing at all for a golden, or mint one nothing
   reads; so the two halves are held to each other by NAME, which is exactly
   the part no later run would catch. -}
toolTableStart : String
toolTableStart = "# ── GOLDEN TABLE BEGIN"

toolTableEnd : String
toolTableEnd = "# ── GOLDEN TABLE END"

toolGoldens : <FileRead "_", IO> Result String (List String)
toolGoldens = match readFile "\{medakaRoot}/test/lsp_bless.sh"
  Err e => Err "cannot read test/lsp_bless.sh: \{e}"
  Ok src => match between toolTableStart toolTableEnd (lines src)
    [] => Err "test/lsp_bless.sh has no GOLDEN TABLE block"
    ls => Ok (sort (filter isName (map trim ls)))

isName : String -> Bool
isName l = l /= "" && not (startsWith "#" l)

between : String -> String -> List String -> List String
between _ _ [] = []
between from to (l :: rest) =
  if startsWith from l then untilLine to rest else between from to rest

untilLine : String -> List String -> List String
untilLine _ [] = []
untilLine to (l :: rest) =
  if startsWith to l then [] else l :: untilLine to rest

-- | The goldens the rows above read, each once. Three rows share the B.10.3
-- session dump, so the list is deduplicated before it is compared.
ownGoldens : List String
ownGoldens = sort (nub (somes (map oracleName probes)))

oracleName : Probe -> Option String
oracleName p = match p.oracle
  NoOracle => None
  Text name => Some name
  Frames name => Some name

test "the bless tool mints exactly the goldens this file reads" =
  match toolGoldens
    Err e => fail e
    Ok minted =>
      if minted == ownGoldens then
        pass
      else
        fail
          "test/lsp_bless.sh and this file disagree about the golden set.\n  the tool mints:\n\{indentAll minted}  this gate reads:\n\{indentAll ownGoldens}"
